                    {
                        "sense_id": "0e8d823c-cf30-30e1-a380-45f1bc74ea1f",
                        "entry_id": "2bf6e82c-151f-306a-93d7-791dcff794fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who bellows."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "033b412f-c4c8-4989-94d2-9632d38db20a",
                                "sense_id": "0e8d823c-cf30-30e1-a380-45f1bc74ea1f",
                                "text": "And these [oxen] the wittie-borne\n(Argicides,) set serious spie vpon:\nSeuering from all the rest; and setting gone\nFull fiftie of the violent Bellowers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eea55653-8c95-4b16-b178-fec5bf6ae186",
                                "sense_id": "0e8d823c-cf30-30e1-a380-45f1bc74ea1f",
                                "text": "1794, Robert Jephson, Roman Portraits, London: G.G. and J. Robinson, lines 558-561, p. 38,\nBesides, the scent of mischief lur’d along\n(The scum of towns) a numerous noisy throng;\nBellowers, unfit to govern or obey,\nWho little heed the cause, but love the fray;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c6f84b8-6300-44ab-bad0-02239aa0dceb",
                                "sense_id": "0e8d823c-cf30-30e1-a380-45f1bc74ea1f",
                                "text": "‘A—hem!’ cried the same voice; and that, not in the tone of an ordinary clearing of the throat, but in a kind of bellow, which woke up all the echoes in the neighbourhood, and was prolonged to an extent which must have made the unseen bellower quite black in the face."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16307352-8d3c-4ce9-a1c5-446d98d65058",
                                "sense_id": "0e8d823c-cf30-30e1-a380-45f1bc74ea1f",
                                "text": "Mic-swinging lead bellower Roger Daltrey stuck to singing, while sometime-vocalist Pete Townshend proved his guitar game was as strong as his aptitude and willingness for pithy, insolent commentary."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
